This is a modified version of the pure-Rust codec2 0.3.1 implementation by
David Rowe and Matt Weeks, https://github.com/scriptjunkie/codec2.
The original manifest declares LGPL-2.1-only AND MIT. The original package
and pinned repository have no separate MIT license file; the original manifest
and README are retained under licenses/. Do not erase the upstream declaration.
Codec2's LGPL-2.1 text and the embedded KISS FFT BSD-3-Clause notice are retained
there as well. Original author/function notices remain in the adapted sources.

Modified for rsLXST on 2026-10-01: bounded storage and scratch; in-place state
initialisation; per-instance synthesis RNG; exact libm math on all targets;
checked public frame shapes; corrected real-FFT input copying; shared the
identical forward FFT plan and removed unreachable mode/rate storage; separated
phase scratch lifetime from inverse FFT scratch for the MCU stack. The public API
exposes native 700C/1600/3200 modes at 8 kHz mono. Other private upstream modes
are not a supported API. See UPSTREAM.json for immutable original provenance.

The native 700C implementation and immutable codebooks additionally adapt
David Rowe's Codec2 C implementation, Copyright 2017, under LGPL-2.1-only:
https://github.com/drowe67/codec2 at commit
310777b1c6f1af0bc7c72f5b32f80f6fd9136962. Source/codebook hashes are recorded in
UPSTREAM.json. Modified for rsLXST on 2026-10-01: Rust newamp1 spectral
quantization and phase reconstruction, fixed M-best scratch and FFT plans,
streamed synthesis models, explicit mode identity, and default 700C settings.
Shared analysis and synthesis preserve reference scalar promotions in pitch,
windows, FFT twiddles, notch filtering and phase arithmetic. KISS FFT changes
retain its BSD-3-Clause attribution. Corrected inherited
background-estimator voicing and pitch-search endpoint/history-bin behavior.

New wrapper, tests and storage adaptation are provided under LGPL-2.1-only.
Third-party libm retains its own MIT license and appears in the workspace's
locked third-party inventory. Packaging must retain the applicable notices and
provide the corresponding modified Codec2 source and relinking materials.
